menu "ULANI BLE"

config ULANI_BLE_ALLOW_PAIRING
    bool "Pair when the calendar demands an encrypted link"
    default y
    help
        The calendar rejects CCCD writes on an unencrypted link with ATT error
        0x05 (insufficient authentication), which is why the reference Node.js
        implementation requires an OS-level pairing first. With this enabled the
        firmware reacts to that rejection by pairing and retrying, so a unit
        that does not care is never bothered. Turn it off to see the raw
        rejection instead.

config ULANI_BLE_SECURE_CONNECTIONS
    bool "Offer LE Secure Connections when pairing"
    default n
    help
        The calendar asks for Secure Connections in its Security Request, but
        answering in kind gets the link dropped without so much as a Pairing
        Response. LE Legacy pairing is spec-legal to offer regardless of what
        the peer advertises and is what 2019-era hardware was actually tested
        against, so it is the default here. Flip this back on if legacy also
        fails, to see which one the device complains about.

config ULANI_BLE_VERBOSE_LOG
    bool "Log every GAP event and the full NimBLE host trace"
    default n
    help
        Raises the ulani_ble and NimBLE tags to DEBUG at startup, which shows
        the security-manager exchange packet by packet. Invaluable when a
        connection will not come up, but do not leave it on: NimBLE logs one
        line per HCI byte, so an image transfer (835 packets of 230 bytes)
        cannot possibly keep up with the timing the panel expects.

config ULANI_BLE_CHUNK_GAP_MS
    int "Delay between image data packets (ms)"
    default 20
    range 0 200
    help
        The reference implementation waits 20 ms between the 230-byte writes
        that make up an image. Raising this makes a transfer slower but can help
        if the panel drops packets while WiFi is busy.

endmenu
